hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"337","A chapter on ransoming with minors, and on one who finds his property among the spoils: Hannad narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent the remainder of the fifth - of the women and offspring - with Sa'id ibn Zayd to Najd, to sell them for him in exchange for horses and weapons. Abu Dawud said: This was mentioned concerning the raid of Qurayzah."
"338","Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Tamim ibn Tarafah, he said: A man found his she-camel in the possession of (another) man, and the two brought the matter to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He established proof that it was his she-camel, and the other established proof that he had bought it from the enemy. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish, take it for what he bought it for, and if you wish, leave it."
